# network_simulation_manager.md.backup

This sanitized note summarizes the Network Simulation Manager without exposing test endpoints or credentials.

## Responsibilities

- Coordinate deterministic state replication between peers in lockstep simulations.
- Buffer outgoing state snapshots and reconcile incoming updates against the current frame.
- Surface lifecycle hooks so gameplay systems can subscribe to connection events.

## Configuration Guidelines

- Network addresses, ports, and protocol details live in external configuration files; do not hardcode sample endpoints in documentation or code.
- Enable or disable server/client roles through initialization flags that can be toggled per build target.
- Keep serialization schemas versioned so mismatched clients fail gracefully.

## Runtime Usage

- Initialize the manager during engine startup, then call `update()` once per frame to process queued packets.
- Retrieve replicated entities through accessor methods that provide immutable snapshots.
- Always validate payload sizes and schema identifiers before applying remote state.
